Carafe Lab: an NCE access that faults on a GPU-cached page tells the GPU caches about each whole page it touches, not
only the bytes it accessed. The host protects whole pages, so a cache that tracks other bytes of the page kept it
protected: the shader cache keeps a page while any shader on it lives, and a guest writing a new shader beside an old
one faulted again until the page was uncached by force, after which the cache never learned of later writes and could
run stale code. Each cache now lets go of the page in its own way, and the forced uncaching is left for pages no cache
tracks at all.
GPL-3.0-or-later, as the file it changes.

